known_limitations:
- Issue 163 external portable runtime-package compilation remains a separate lane.
- Issue 169 Grade-9 exit readiness remains a separate route and is not claimed by
  the learner-page builder.
discoveries:
- The production learner host can consume real Issue 173 compiler output and Issue
  174 Motion canonical data without browser-side curriculum discovery.
- A pre-existing scientific explorer can be mounted unchanged through explicit canonical
  resource metadata while pedagogy remains projection-driven.
- PR 134 demonstrates why standalone page-local diagnostics must not become the builder's
  second academic database.
handoff:
  what_changed:
  - The existing Issue 175 shell/host-parity work is now backed by production compiler-generated
    Motion Core projections.
  - Public and standalone hosts mount the existing shared-clock explorer through explicit
    generated metadata.
  - PR 134 is dispositioned and closed unmerged as a reference prototype.
  what_is_true_now:
  - One generated shell covers Core1A/Core1B/Core2A/Core2B using explicit projection
    state.
  - Core2A visibly distinguishes the crux after attempt/reveal.
  - Core2B protected decisions remain undisclosed before attempt.
  - Public/standalone parity and offline same-origin explorer mounting are tested.
  - Accepted material head is b8a96923383aa1f7fdf4d6eb2a6c866225570a21.
  what_remains_uncertain:
  - External portable/single-file packaging and cross-subject portability proofs belong
    to Issue 163.
  do_not_break:
  - Do not add page-local curriculum, question-bank, mastery or support-policy truth.
  - Do not move compiler/raw subject discovery into the browser runtime.
  - Do not rewrite scientific explorer implementations merely to fit the generated
    shell.
  attempted_and_rejected:
  - Merging PR 134 as-is was rejected because it combines scientific scene, prediction
    choices, diagnostics and correctness/feedback logic in one page-local model.
  resume_from:
  - Deliver PR 178 through V3 provider transition.
  - Then proceed to Issue 163 external portability without transferring learner-shell
    ownership into that lane.
  first_successor_action: If PR 178 is merged, close Issue 175 after V3 provider readback
    and admit the next independent portability task.
